sum='Two friends exchange letters. Soumya from Bengaluru writes to Ananda in Chandigarh about her school trip to the National War Memorial, New Delhi – built from April 2018 to February 2019 over 40 acres near India Gate and inaugurated by Prime Minister Narendra Modi. Its 29,000 tablets carry the names of over 26,000 soldiers who made the supreme sacrifice in wars since 1947. She describes the 21 Param Vir Chakra awardees, the first being Major Somnath Sharma (Battle of Badgam, 1947), the citation of Lance Naik Albert Ekka (1971, Gangasagar), the Amar Jawan Jyoti in the obelisk, and the four concentric chakras – Amar (immortality), Veerta (bravery), Tyag (sacrifice) and Raksha (protection). She will present the story of Major Padmapani Acharya (MVC, Kargil 1999). Ananda replies that a war memorial is an expression of deep gratitude; she recalls the war memorial in Chandigarh’s Bougainvillea Garden, the poem “Pushp ki Abhilasha”, Captain Anuj Nayyar (MVC, Kargil), the National War Memorial and Museum app, and her hobby of collecting stamps (philately). She is inspired to join the Armed Forces.',
